t is self-contained and delivered in-session.\n\nRead: ~282\n\n**General**\n| ID | Time | T | Title | Read | Work |\n|----|------|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#526** \" 🔵 **wttr.in Weather Fetch Failed with Exit Code 52 During Morning Briefing**\n\nDuring the 7 AM morning briefing execution for Sam, the weather skill attempted to fetch current Seoul conditions from wttr.in. The curl process (session ember-shoal, pid 52163) exited with code 52, indicating the server accepted the connection but returned an empty reply. This is a transient or rate-limiting issue with wttr.in. The briefing's weather section would have been unavailable or fallback text used. Worth noting in case this recurs — wttr.in can occasionally be unreliable or rate-limit automated requests.\n\nRead: ~274\n\n**General**\n| ID | Time | T | Title | Read | Work |\n|----|------|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#527** 7:01 AM 🔵 **Second wttr.in Fetch Also Terminated During Morning Briefing**\n\nA second attempt to fetch Seoul weather from wttr.in also failed — the process ran for over 20 seconds with no output before being explicitly terminated. Combined with the first attempt exiting with code 52 (empty server reply), wttr.in appears to have been fully unresponsive during Sam's morning briefing on 2026-02-25. The morning briefing's weather section was unavailable. If this recurs, consider adding a fallback weather source (e.g., Open-Meteo, which is also listed as an option in the weather skill) or a timeout with graceful degradation.\n\nRead: ~266\n\n**General**\n| ID | Time | T | Title | Read | Work |\n|----|------|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#528** \" 🔵 **web_fetch Also Failed for Weather During Morning Briefing**\n\nAfter two curl-based attempts to wttr.in failed, a web_fetch call was also attempted and returned a generic \"fetch failed\" error. This confirms that weather data retrieval was entirely unavailable during Sam's 7 AM Seoul briefing on 2026-02-25 — likely due to network-level issues or wttr.in downtime. All three fetch strategies failed. The briefing proceeded without weather data.\n\nRead: ~219\n\n\nAccess 112k tokens of past research & decisions for just 19,146t. Use the claude-mem skill to access memories by ID."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771970503355}}
